Package: xios-fonts-noto
Name: Noto Sans fonts
Version: 1.0.1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Google / Noto project
Depends: fontconfig
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: Noto Sans, the font KDE actually asks for
 KDE Plasma's built-in default UI font is "Noto Sans" (and "Noto Sans Mono" for
 fixed width). iOS ships ~120 Noto faces under /System/Library/Fonts, but they
 are script-specific Unicode-support faces (Noto Sans Newa, Noto Sans Sora
 Sompeng, ...) -- there is no plain "Noto Sans" family. So every KDE app asked
 fontconfig for a family that did not exist and got Verdana back, which is why
 text rendered wrong across the desktop.
 .
 This ships the real Noto Sans, Noto Sans Italic and Noto Sans Mono variable
 fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, see /var/jb/usr/share/doc/xios-fonts-noto).
 It does not change any fontconfig defaults: x11-fonts-sf still maps the generic
 sans-serif/monospace aliases to San Francisco. This only makes the explicit
 "Noto Sans" family resolve to Noto Sans.
